lord|nobleman|NOUN|man with a noble title or authority|A man with a noble title or authority over land and people in a historical setting.|lãnh chúa; quý tộc có tước vị|The story begins when a local lord gives the mill to the village.|Câu chuyện bắt đầu khi một lãnh chúa địa phương trao cối xay cho dân làng.|Countable; Lord is capitalized when used as a title before a name. Religious uses of the Lord have a different context.|0
rid|remove-an-unwanted-thing|VERB|free from something unwanted|To free a person or place from something unwanted.|loại bỏ; làm cho thoát khỏi|Clearing the gutters helped rid the roof of trapped leaves.|Việc làm sạch máng xối giúp loại bỏ lá mắc lại trên mái nhà.|Rid someone or something of something; rid is used as both base and past form, and ridded also occurs. Get rid of is a related idiomatic expression.|0
sunlight|light-from-the-sun|NOUN|light coming from the sun|Light that comes from the sun.|ánh nắng; ánh sáng mặt trời|Sunlight reached the kitchen table through a gap in the curtains.|Ánh nắng chiếu tới bàn bếp qua một khe hở giữa những tấm rèm.|Uncountable; in sunlight or a beam of sunlight. Sunlight describes the light rather than the heat it may produce.|-
writing|producing-text|NOUN|activity of producing written text|The activity of forming written words or composing text.|việc viết; hoạt động viết lách|Writing the exhibition labels took longer than arranging the photographs.|Việc viết nhãn cho triển lãm mất nhiều thời gian hơn việc sắp xếp các bức ảnh.|Uncountable for the activity; writing about a topic identifies its subject. Writings can instead refer to collected works.|0
writing|handwriting|NOUN|visible handwritten words|Words or letters written by hand, or the way they are formed.|chữ viết; nét chữ|The writing on the postcard was too small for me to read easily.|Chữ viết trên tấm bưu thiếp quá nhỏ nên tôi không dễ đọc được.|Uncountable in this sense; neat or clear writing describes the letter shapes. Distinct from the activity of composing text.|1
competence|ability-to-do-well|NOUN|ability to do something adequately|The ability to carry out a task well enough to meet its requirements.|năng lực; khả năng thực hiện thành thạo|The supervisor assessed her competence in handling customer enquiries.|Người giám sát đánh giá năng lực xử lý các yêu cầu của khách hàng của cô.|Usually uncountable; competence in an activity or to do something. Competencies can name particular skills in professional frameworks.|0
